                                            <passage><![CDATA[Abraham Lincoln was one of the greatest presidents of the United States.  He prevented the United States from splitting into two countries during the American Civil War, and won a long battle to prevent the spread of slavery.  Lincoln was able to talk so clearly and forcefully and was so sincere that he persuaded many people to support his ideas.<br/><br/>Lincoln was the son of a simple farmer and carpenter.  His birthplace was a log cabin on his father's farm in Kentucky.  As a boy he worked hard on the farm and spent less than a year at school.  In 1831 he left home for New Orleans.  He moved to a village called New Salem, where he became a clerk in a shop.  After a few months the shop was closed and Lincoln tried various occupations.<br/><br/>In 1834 Lincoln was elected to the state government.  The same year he started to study law, and he practiced as a lawyer for some years.  In 1847 he was elected for two years to the House of Representatives.<br/><br/>One of Lincoln's chief assets as a politician was his reputation for honesty.  In 1835 Lincoln and William Berry bought a store on credit.  It did not go well and the debts began to mount up.  Then Berry died and Lincoln was left with debts of over a thousand dollars.  Lincoln worked hard and eventually paid all of his debts.  This gave rise to his nickname of 'Honest Abe' that was to stay with him for the rest of his life.<br/><br/>In 1854 the law limiting the amount of slavery changed.  Lincoln thought slavery was evil and joined the Republican Party, which opposed it.  In 1860 he was elected president, but nearly all his votes came from the northern states.  Ten southern states decided to set up their own union, called the Confederate States. They wanted to govern themselves.<br/><br/>The next year the American Civil War broke out between the Confederate states and the states that remained part of the Union.  Lincoln stated that his aim in the war was to preserve the union, not to end slavery.  Lincoln was re-elected president in 1864 and the Confederates surrendered shortly afterwards.  But he did not live to see the southern states re-joined to the north.  A few days after the end of the war he was shot dead in a Washington theater. ]]></passage>


                                            <en_script_sentence><![CDATA[***Abraham Lincoln was one of the greatest presidents of the United States.*** ***He prevented the United States from splitting into two countries during the American Civil War, and won a long battle to prevent the spread of slavery.*** ***Lincoln was able to talk so clearly and forcefully and was so sincere that he persuaded many people to support his ideas.***

***Lincoln was the son of a simple farmer and carpenter.*** ***His birthplace was a log cabin on his father's farm in Kentucky.*** ***As a boy he worked hard on the farm and spent less than a year at school.*** ***In 1831 he left home for New Orleans.*** ***He moved to a village called New Salem, where he became a clerk in a shop.*** ***After a few months the shop was closed and Lincoln tried various occupations.***

***In 1834 Lincoln was elected to the state government.*** ***The same year he started to study law, and he practiced as a lawyer for some years.*** ***In 1847 he was elected for two years to the House of Representatives.***

***One of Lincoln's chief assets as a politician was his reputation for honesty.*** ***In 1835 Lincoln and William Berry bought a store on credit.*** ***It did not go well and the debts began to mount up.*** ***Then Berry died and Lincoln was left with debts of over a thousand dollars.*** ***Lincoln worked hard and eventually paid all of his debts.*** ***This gave rise to his nickname of 'Honest Abe' that was to stay with him for the rest of his life.***

***In 1854 the law limiting the amount of slavery changed.*** ***Lincoln thought slavery was evil and joined the Republican Party, which opposed it.*** ***In 1860 he was elected president, but nearly all his votes came from the northern states.*** ***Ten southern states decided to set up their own union, called the Confederate States.*** ***They wanted to govern themselves.***

***The next year the American Civil War broke out between the Confederate states and the states that remained part of the Union.*** ***Lincoln stated that his aim in the war was to preserve the union, not to end slavery.*** ***Lincoln was re-elected president in 1864 and the Confederates surrendered shortly afterwards.*** ***But he did not live to see the southern states re-joined to the north.*** ***A few days after the end of the war he was shot dead in a Washington theater. ***]]></en_script_sentence>

                                        <jp_script><![CDATA[　アブラハム・リンカーンは合衆国の最も偉大な大統領のひとりだった。彼は、合衆国がアメリカ南北戦争の間に２つの国に分裂するのを防ぎ、そして、奴隷制度の広がりを妨ぐための長い戦いに勝利した。リンカーンは非常にはっきりと力強く話すことができ、非常に誠実だったので、多くの人々を促して彼の考えを支持させることができた。<br/><br/>　リンカーンは単なる農夫と大工の息子だった。彼の生まれた場所は、ケンタッキーの父親の農場の丸太小屋だった。少年の頃、彼はその農場で一生懸命働き、学校に通ったのは１年よりも少なかった。１８３１年に、彼は家を離れニューオリンズに向かった。彼はニューサレムと呼ばれる村に移り、そしてそこで、ある店の店員になった。数ヵ月後、その店は閉店し、リンカーンはさまざまな仕事をやってみた。<br/><br/>　１８３４年に、リンカーンは州議会に選ばれた。同年、彼は法律を勉強しはじめ、数年間、弁護士として開業した。１８４７年、彼は２年間下院に選ばれた。<br/><br/>　リンカーンの政治家としての主な長所のひとつは、正直であるという評判だった。１８３５年、リンカーンとウィリアム・ベリーはひとつの店を掛買いした。それはうまくいかなかったので、借金がかさみはじめた。その後、ベリーは死に、リンカーンは１０００ドル以上の借金を背負わされた。リンカーンは一生懸命働き、結局は借金のすべてを返済した。このことが、彼の残りの人生について回ることになった『オネスト（正直者の）エイブ』というあだ名を生み出した。<br/><br/>　１８５４年、奴隷の数を限定する法律が変わった。リンカーンは、奴隷制度は悪いことだと思い、共和党に入った、その党はそれに反対していた。１８６０年に、彼は大統領に選ばれたが、しかし、彼のほとんどすべての票は、北部の州からのものだった。南部の１０州が、南部連合国と呼ばれる、彼ら自身の連合を創設しようと決意した。彼らは自分たちで統治したいと思った。<br/><br/>　その翌年、アメリカ南北戦争が、南部連合国と依然として合衆国（北部連合）の一部のままであった諸州の間（北軍）に勃発した。リンカーンは、その戦争で彼の目的は、奴隷制度を終わらせることではなく、連合を保つことであると述べた。リンカーンは１８６４年に大統領に再選され、南部連合国はその後まもなく降伏した。しかし、彼は南部の州が北部に再び加えられるのを見ずに亡くなった。終戦の数日後、彼はワシントン劇場で撃ち殺された。]]></jp_script>

